# Citation File Format v1.2.0 — https://citation-file-format.github.io/
# GitHub renders this as a "Cite this repository" button on the repo page.
# Zenodo reads this file on release to mint a DOI and populate deposit metadata.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this dataset, schema, or methodology in academic or policy work,
  please cite it using the metadata below. Prefer the DOI once one is minted
  via the Zenodo integration (first tagged release).
title: "Cross-Layer Censorship Event Database"
abstract: >-
  A working event corpus for two linked research arms: domain analysis of
  cross-layer crypto restrictions and recovery, and measurement analysis of
  coverage, source support, and coding error. Records link public triggers,
  targets, six observation surfaces, and source anchors. Existing admission
  and reaction labels are provisional legacy coding, including a separately
  marked secondary-evidence tier; hashes establish source integrity rather
  than semantic truth. Independent human validation and a bounded measurement
  cohort remain pending. Data/documentation use CC-BY-4.0; software uses MIT.
type: dataset
version: "0.2.0-rc-dryrun-11"
